== Disposition

This report details every stage of the project from conceptualisation to successful completion. It follows a logical structure and outlines the major stages in chronological order. A brief summary of each section is presented in the list below.

- @sec:introduction - #strong[Introduction] \ #emph[Introduces the concept of decompilation and its applications, outlines the project aim and objectives, and summarises its deliverables.]

- @sec:literature_review - #strong[Literature Review] \ #emph[Details the problem domain, reviews traditional decompilation techniques, and evaluates potential intermediate representations for the decompilation pipeline of the project.]

- @sec:related_work - #strong[Related Work] \ #emph[Evaluates projects for translating native code to LLVM IR, and reviews the design of modern decompilers.]

- @sec:methodology - #strong[Methodology] \ #emph[Surveys methodologies and best practices for software construction, and relates them to the specific problem domain.]

- @sec:requirements - #strong[Requirements] \ #emph[Specifies and prioritises the requirements of the project artefacts.]

- @sec:design - #strong[Design] \ #emph[Discusses the system architecture and the design of each component, motivates the choice of core algorithms and data structures, and highlights strengths and limitations of the design.]

- @sec:implementation - #strong[Implementation] \ #emph[Discusses language considerations, describes the implementation process, and showcases how set-backs were dealt with.]

- @sec:verification - #strong[Verification] \ #emph[Describes the approaches taken to validate the correctness, performance and security of the artefacts.]

- @sec:evaluation - #strong[Evaluation] \ #emph[Assesses the outcome of the project and evaluates the artefacts against the requirements.]

- @sec:conclusion - #strong[Conclusion] \ #emph[Summarises the project outcomes, presents ideas for future work, reflects on personal development, and concludes with an attribution to the key idea of this project.]
